      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "International organizations often face obstacles because they operate based on consensus among member states, which heavily favors powerful nations. Geopolitical interests and member state veto power frequently override humanitarian concerns or the specific needs of smaller countries. Furthermore, the principle of national sovereignty itself often shields governments from meaningful intervention, limiting the organizations' enforcement capability. Ultimately, the organization's mandate is diluted by the competing political agendas of its most powerful members.",
